{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "94d555dc-a3d5-5bcc-a939-d06c396c4241",
    "name": "CarRentals",
    "description": "Car Rentals (KM2). Proces wynajmu w naszym Car Rental API (lokalnie, http://localhost:5080) i podstawowe wywołania Broker API (http://localhost:5100).\n\nJak uruchomić:\n1. docker compose up --build (z katalogu głównego repo) albo dotnet run obu API.\n2. W Postmanie Import: ta kolekcja i environment local (docs/postman/local.postman_environment.json), wybrać environment local.\n3. Folder \"Car Rental API: proces wynajmu\" uruchomić w Runnerze w kolejności. Krok 6 czeka 15 s na potwierdzenie w tle.\n4. Potem folder \"Car Rental API: bezpieczeństwo\" i \"Broker API\".\n\nZmienne offerId i rentalId ustawiają się same w zakładce Tests.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Car Rental API: proces wynajmu",
      "description": "Lista aut, oferta, wynajem, status po 10 s, zwrot, potwierdzenie zwrotu przez pracownika. Uruchamiać po kolei (Runner).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Lista aut",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "x-api-key",
                "value": "{{apiKey}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "cars"
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const cars = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"lista ma 12 aut z seeda\", () => pm.expect(cars).to.be.an(\"array\").with.lengthOf(12));",
                  "pm.test(\"auto ma id, make, model, year, location, available\", () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(cars[0]).to.include.all.keys(\"id\", \"make\", \"model\", \"year\", \"location\", \"available\");",
                  "});",
                  "// Bierzemy pierwsze auto z Warszawy (oferta musi być w mieście auta)",
                  "const car = cars.find(c => c.location === \"Warszawa\") || cars[0];",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"carId\", car.id);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"carLocation\", car.location);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Szczegóły auta",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "x-api-key",
                "value": "{{apiKey}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/cars/{{carId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "cars",
                "{{carId}}"
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"to samo auto\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().id).to.eql(Number(pm.collectionVariables.get(\"carId\"))));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Oferta (wycena)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "x-api-key",
                "value": "{{apiKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/offers",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "offers"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"carId\": {{carId}},\n  \"age\": 30,\n  \"licenseYears\": 10,\n  \"location\": \"{{carLocation}}\",\n  \"startDate\": \"{{startDate}}\",\n  \"endDate\": \"{{endDate}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Termin daleko w przyszłości i losowy, żeby kolejne przebiegi nie trafiały na zajęte auto (409)",
                  "const offset = 40 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 300);",
                  "const start = new Date();",
                  "start.setUTCDate(start.getUTCDate() + offset);",
                  "const end = new Date(start);",
                  "end.setUTCDate(end.getUTCDate() + 3);",
                  "const fmt = d => d.toISOString().slice(0, 10);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"startDate\", fmt(start));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"endDate\", fmt(end));"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"201 Created\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const offer = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"jest offerId, ceny i termin ważności\", () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(offer).to.include.all.keys(\"offerId\", \"dailyPrice\", \"dailyInsurancePrice\", \"totalPrice\", \"currency\", \"days\", \"expiresAt\");",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test(\"cena całkowita = (cena dzienna + ubezpieczenie) razy dni\", () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(offer.totalPrice).to.be.closeTo((offer.dailyPrice + offer.dailyInsurancePrice) * offer.days, 0.01);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test(\"oferta ważna co najmniej 9,5 minuty\", () => {",
                  "    const minutes = (new Date(offer.expiresAt) - new Date()) / 60000;",
                  "    pm.expect(minutes).to.be.above(9.5);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"offerId\", offer.offerId);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "4. Wniosek o wynajem",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "x-api-key",
                "value": "{{apiKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/rentals",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "rentals"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"offerId\": \"{{offerId}}\",\n  \"firstName\": \"Jan\",\n  \"lastName\": \"Kowalski\",\n  \"email\": \"{{customerEmail}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"202 Accepted\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(202));",
                  "const rental = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"status Pending\", () => pm.expect(rental.status).to.eql(\"Pending\"));",
                  "pm.test(\"jest rentalId\", () => pm.expect(rental.rentalId).to.be.a(\"string\").and.not.empty);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"rentalId\", rental.rentalId);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "5. Status zaraz po wniosku",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "x-api-key",
                "value": "{{apiKey}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/rentals/{{rentalId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "rentals",
                "{{rentalId}}"
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"wniosek jeszcze czeka (Pending)\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql(\"Pending\"));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "6. Status po 10 s",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "x-api-key",
                "value": "{{apiKey}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/rentals/{{rentalId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "rentals",
                "{{rentalId}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Czeka 15 s w Pre-request (10 s opóźnienia potwierdzenia + do 5 s na kolejne sprawdzenie bazy przez proces w tle)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Proces w tle potwierdza wniosek po 10 s i sprawdza bazę co 5 s, więc czekamy 15 s",
                  "setTimeout(() => {}, 15000);"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"wynajem potwierdzony (Confirmed)\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql(\"Confirmed\"));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
